# Contribution Log — Bubble Sort Profiling System

## 1. Purpose

This log records the implementation and documentation work for the Bubble Sort Profiling System. The project compares unoptimized Bubble Sort with an optimized version and documents the design using four C4 Model diagrams.

## 2. Algorithm Work

### Unoptimized implementation

- Implemented `bubble_sort_unoptimized(arr)` with nested loops.
- Compared adjacent array elements.
- Swapped elements when they were in the wrong order.
- Kept the standard pass structure without an early-stop check.

### Optimized implementation

- Implemented `bubble_sort_optimized(arr)`.
- Added a `swapped` flag for each pass.
- Set the flag when a swap occurred.
- Added a `break` condition when a complete pass made no swaps.

This optimization improves the best-case time complexity to `O(N)`. Average and worst-case time complexity remain `O(N²)`.

## 3. Workload and Benchmarking

- Configured the array size to 3,000 integers.
- Configured 10 runs/datasets.
- Generated random integers in the range 1 to 100,000.
- Reused the same base datasets for both implementations.
- Passed a copy of each dataset to the sorting function.
- Measured each implementation's total elapsed time using Python's `time` module.
- Printed the total time for both implementations.

Timing values are generated by running the program and are not fixed in this log.

